{keys:['healthy','normal','healthy leaf'],title:'Healthy plant',cause:'The model classified the image as healthy. A single photo cannot guarantee that the whole plant is disease-free.',risk:'Continue monitoring; early infections can be difficult to see.',solution:'Keep good field hygiene, use clean planting material and inspect plants regularly.',advice:'Take clear photos of both sides of leaves if new symptoms appear.'},
{keys:['fall armyworm','army worm','spodoptera'],title:'Fall armyworm (maize pest)',cause:'Larvae of Spodoptera frugiperda feed inside the maize whorl and can damage leaves, tassels and cobs.',risk:'Severe infestations can reduce yield and spread quickly between fields.',solution:'Scout fields frequently, destroy egg masses/young larvae where practical and ask an agronomist about locally registered integrated pest-management options.',advice:'Do not apply a pesticide based only on this photo; follow product labels and local extension advice.'},
{keys:['cassava mosaic','cmd'],title:'Cassava mosaic disease',cause:'A viral disease spread mainly by whiteflies and infected cassava cuttings.',risk:'Leaf mosaic, distortion and stunting can reduce root yield substantially.',solution:'Use healthy planting material and locally recommended resistant/tolerant varieties; remove infected plants according to local extension guidance.',advice:'Ask RAB or a district agronomist to confirm the diagnosis and obtain clean cuttings.'},
{keys:['cassava brown streak','cbsd'],title:'Cassava brown streak disease',cause:'A viral disease spread by whiteflies and infected planting material; roots may develop brown necrotic patches.',risk:'Root damage may be serious even when above-ground symptoms are subtle.',solution:'Use clean cuttings and varieties recommended by local agricultural authorities; manage affected plants with extension guidance.',advice:'Do not move cuttings from suspected infected plants.'},
{keys:['late blight','phytophthora'],title:'Potato late blight',cause:'Caused by Phytophthora infestans; cool, wet and humid conditions favour rapid spread.',risk:'Can destroy foliage and tubers quickly in favourable weather.',solution:'Use healthy seed tubers, remove volunteer potato plants, avoid moving infected tubers and seek locally approved control guidance.',advice:'After wet weather, inspect leaves and stems frequently and contact an agronomist promptly.'},
{keys:['early blight','alternaria'],title:'Early blight',cause:'A fungal disease commonly associated with Alternaria species; older leaves may develop brown target-like spots.',risk:'Severe leaf loss can reduce plant vigour and yield.',solution:'Rotate crops, remove heavily infected debris, avoid prolonged leaf wetness and ask extension staff about registered treatments.',advice:'Confirm the crop and symptoms before selecting a treatment.'},
{keys:['bacterial wilt','ralstonia'],title:'Bacterial wilt',cause:'A soil- and water-associated bacterial disease that can block water movement in the plant.',risk:'Can cause rapid wilting and persist in contaminated soil or planting material.',solution:'Use clean planting material, avoid moving soil/water from affected plots and follow local sanitation and rotation advice.',advice:'There is no safe universal home cure; get an agronomist to confirm the diagnosis.'},
{keys:['anthracnose'],title:'Anthracnose',cause:'A fungal disease that can cause dark, sunken lesions on leaves, stems, pods or fruits depending on the crop.',risk:'May damage marketable produce and reduce yield in wet conditions.',solution:'Use clean seed/planting material, rotate crops, remove infected residues and improve airflow where suitable.',advice:'Ask an agronomist to distinguish it from other leaf-spot diseases.'},
{keys:['bacterial spot'],title:'Bacterial spot',cause:'A bacterial disease that can cause small dark lesions on leaves and fruit.',risk:'Wet weather and splashing water can spread infection.',solution:'Avoid working among wet plants, use clean transplants/seed and follow crop rotation and sanitation guidance.',advice:'Do not reuse a treatment recommendation from a different crop without expert confirmation.'},
{keys:['leaf mold'],title:'Leaf mold',cause:'A fungal disease favoured by humid conditions, especially in dense or poorly ventilated foliage.',risk:'Yellowing and leaf loss may reduce growth and yield.',solution:'Improve airflow, avoid wetting foliage when possible and remove affected debris.',advice:'Confirm the plant species and disease before applying any fungicide.'},
{keys:['septoria leaf spot','septoria'],title:'Septoria leaf spot',cause:'A fungal leaf disease that produces many small dark spots, often on older leaves.',risk:'Severe infection can cause leaf drop and reduce yield.',solution:'Rotate crops, remove infected debris, avoid overhead irrigation where practical and seek local advice about registered control.',advice:'Inspect the lower leaves and nearby plants; confirm the crop before treatment.'},
{keys:['yellow leaf curl virus','tomato yellow leaf curl'],title:'Tomato yellow leaf curl virus',cause:'A viral disease of tomato commonly spread by whiteflies.',risk:'Leaf curling, yellowing and stunting can reduce fruit production.',solution:'Use locally recommended resistant varieties and healthy seedlings; manage whiteflies through integrated, locally approved practices.',advice:'Ask an agronomist to confirm the virus and avoid moving suspect seedlings.'},
{keys:['mosaic virus','tomato mosaic'],title:'Mosaic virus',cause:'A plant virus that can cause mottled leaves, distortion and reduced growth; transmission varies by virus and crop.',risk:'Plant growth and yield can be reduced, and some viruses spread through contaminated tools or planting material.',solution:'Use clean seed/planting material, clean tools and follow crop-specific sanitation advice from extension staff.',advice:'Do not assume every mosaic pattern is the same virus; get the crop and symptoms confirmed.'},
{keys:['spider mite','spider mites','two spotted spider'],title:'Spider mites',cause:'Tiny mites feed on plant cells and may cause stippling, bronzing and fine webbing, especially in hot, dry conditions.',risk:'Large populations can cause leaf damage and reduce plant vigour.',solution:'Inspect leaf undersides, reduce plant stress, preserve beneficial insects and ask extension staff about locally approved integrated management.',advice:'Do not spray without identifying the pest and checking local recommendations.'},
{keys:['target spot'],title:'Target spot',cause:'A fungal disease that can produce brown circular lesions on leaves and sometimes fruit.',risk:'Leaf damage can reduce plant health and marketable yield.',solution:'Improve airflow, avoid prolonged leaf wetness, rotate crops and remove infected debris.',advice:'Confirm the crop and diagnosis with an agronomist before treatment.'}
